Here is the commit message:
fix ci error introduced by 6862f13bd

Here is the root cause:
The bug was likely caused by the incorrect placement of the highlighting logic within the `mChartTouchListener`, which may have led to improper handling of touch events and highlighting of chart values. The removal of unnecessary imports and the restructuring of the `performHighlight` method indicate that the previous implementation was not correctly encapsulated, resulting in a failure to highlight values as intended.

Here is the patch:
 import android.util.AttributeSet;
 import android.view.MotionEvent;
-import android.view.View;

 import com.github.mikephil.charting.charts.PieChart;
 import com.github.mikephil.charting.highlight.Highlight;
-import com.github.mikephil.charting.listener.ChartTouchListener;
-import com.github.mikephil.charting.listener.OnChartGestureListener;
 import com.github.mikephil.charting.listener.PieRadarChartTouchListener;


     @Override
     protected void init() {
         super.init();

         mChartTouchListener = new PieRadarChartTouchListener(this){

-            if (h != null && !h.equalTo(mLastHighlighted)) {
-                mChart.highlightValue(h, true);
-                mLastHighlighted = h;
+            protected void performHighlight(Highlight h, MotionEvent e) {
+
+                if (h != null && !h.equalTo(mLastHighlighted)) {
+                    mChart.highlightValue(h, true);
+                    mLastHighlighted = h;
+                }
             }
         };
     }
 }


